# Neuralscape — local development environment template
#
# 1. Copy to .env:           cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill in GOOGLE_API_KEY  (the only field that must change for `docker compose up` to work).
# 3. Adjust other settings only if you have a reason to.
#
# For production deployment behind a public domain, see .env.production
# instead — it adds REDIS_PASSWORD, NEURALSCAPE_API_KEY, DOMAIN, and tighter
# defaults.
#
# Every variable here maps to a field on neuralscape-service/config.py
# (Settings class). Pydantic Settings reads them case-insensitively.

# ─── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Gemini API key. Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey.
# Used by mem0's LLM + embedder, Graphiti's LLM + embedder + reranker.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Neo4j auth. The default below matches docker-compose.yml's NEO4J_AUTH
# default so the stack starts cleanly. Change for any non-local deployment.
NEO4J_PASSWORD=neuralscape

# ─── Service URLs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# When you `docker compose up`, the values here are overridden inside the
# containers (REDIS_URL → redis://redis:6379 etc.) by docker-compose.yml.
# These values matter only when running the API/worker locally outside
# Docker (e.g. `uv run python main.py` against a partial docker stack).

REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
QDRANT_URL=http://localhost:6333
NEO4J_URI=neo4j://127.0.0.1:7687
NEO4J_USER=neo4j
NEO4J_DATABASE=memory

# ─── Auth (optional for local single-user dev) ─────────────────────
#
# Two token formats supported. When *neither* is set, auth is disabled
# entirely (the API behaves like the pre-multi-user days). On any public
# deployment you MUST set NEURALSCAPE_USER_TOKEN_SECRET — without it your
# memory layer is wide open to anyone who can reach the host.

# Preferred: per-user HMAC tokens. The server signs tokens with this
# secret; each token carries a user_id the server trusts authoritatively
# (request body user_id is ignored). Issue tokens with:
#   docker exec neuralscape-neuralscape-1 \
#       python scripts/issue_user_token.py -u <user> --days 365
# Generate a fresh 32-byte base64 secret in PowerShell:
#   $b = New-Object byte[] 32
#   [System.Security.Cryptography.RandomNumberGenerator]::Create().GetBytes($b)
#   [Convert]::ToBase64String($b)
NEURALSCAPE_USER_TOKEN_SECRET=

# Legacy: single shared API key. Pre-multi-user shape. When set, any
# bearer matching this exact string is accepted but request.state.user_id
# is NOT populated — routes fall back to body user_id (trust-based).
# Responses carry an X-Neuralscape-Deprecation header. Prefer the per-user
# token above; only set this if you're keeping an old client alive.
NEURALSCAPE_API_KEY=

# ─── OAuth connector (Claude Cowork / claude.ai) ───────────────────
#
# Public HTTPS base URL this service is reachable at from the internet
# (typically your cloudflared hostname). When this is set *together with*
# NEURALSCAPE_USER_TOKEN_SECRET, the service turns on a built-in OAuth 2.1
# Authorization Server so Claude Cowork / claude.ai can add Neuralscape as a
# custom MCP connector with a "Connect → log in" flow (the connector UI has
# no field for a static Bearer token, so OAuth is the only first-class path).
# Leave EMPTY for local dev / Claude Code CLI — OAuth discovery stays off and
# the .well-known/oauth-* endpoints return 404. No trailing slash. See COWORK.md.
NEURALSCAPE_PUBLIC_URL=
# OAuth token lifetimes (seconds). Anthropic silently refreshes, so the access
# token can be short. Defaults: 1h access, 30d refresh. Usually leave unset.
# OAUTH_ACCESS_TTL=3600
# OAUTH_REFRESH_TTL=2592000

# ─── Login provider (who the consent screen authenticates) ─────────
#
# Selects HOW a human proves identity at the OAuth "Connect → log in" step.
# The OAuth machinery above (DCR, codes, access/refresh tokens) is identical
# for every provider — only the login UX changes. Pre-issued admin HMAC tokens
# (issue_user_token.py) keep working as Bearer credentials regardless, so
# CLI/CI/e2e are unaffected. Per-deployment switch:
#   token    → paste an admin-issued HMAC token (default; needs nothing below)
#   google   → "Sign in with Google", gated by the env allowlist
#   supabase → "Sign in with Google" via Supabase, gated by Supabase's
#              Before-User-Created hook (+ optional env allowlist)
AUTH_PROVIDER=token

# Identity: verified email → Neuralscape user_id. Unmapped emails are slugified
# (user_id can't contain "@"; e.g. a@example.com → a-example.com).
# Map known users to existing ids to preserve their memories. Comma-separated
# "email:user_id" pairs.
# AUTH_IDENTITY_MAP=alice@example.com:alice,ops@example.com:ops-bot

# Email allowlist — the gate for AUTH_PROVIDER=google (an optional extra gate
# for supabase). A login passes when the verified email's DOMAIN is allowed OR
# the exact ADDRESS is allowed. Both comma-separated, case-insensitive. An
# empty allowlist denies everyone (fail-closed).
# AUTH_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=example.com
# AUTH_EMAIL_ALLOWLIST=guest@gmail.com,contractor@example.com

# ── AUTH_PROVIDER=google ── (also requires NEURALSCAPE_PUBLIC_URL + _SECRET)
# Google Cloud → Credentials → OAuth client (Web). Authorized redirect URI:
#   {NEURALSCAPE_PUBLIC_URL}/oauth/google/callback
# Consent screen: External + publish (scopes openid/email/profile are
# non-sensitive, so no Google verification review is needed).
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── AUTH_PROVIDER=supabase ── (also requires NEURALSCAPE_PUBLIC_URL + _SECRET)
# Add a Supabase Google provider; in the dashboard set the redirect allow-list
# to include {NEURALSCAPE_PUBLIC_URL}/oauth/supabase/callback. Manage who may
# sign up with a Before-User-Created hook + a signup_email_domains table.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://YOURPROJECT.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Verify the returned session JWT: set the legacy HS256 secret, OR leave empty
# to verify against the project's asymmetric JWKS (derived from SUPABASE_URL).
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=

# ─── Gemini model overrides (optional) ─────────────────────────────

GEMINI_LLM_MODEL=gemini-3-flash-preview
GEMINI_LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
GEMINI_EMBEDDER_MODEL=gemini-embedding-001

# ─── MCP transport ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# stdio — the MCP server runs as a subprocess (good for Claude Desktop's
#         direct stdio config).
# http  — mounts the MCP server on the API at /mcp/ as Streamable HTTP.
#         Required when the neuralscape-plugin's bundled .mcp.json is in
#         use, since it points at <URL>/mcp/. docker-compose.yml sets this
#         to http for both API and worker.
MCP_TRANSPORT=stdio

# ─── Conversation compiler / Obsidian vault ────────────────────────

# Host path the conversation_compiler extension writes notes into
# (Daily logs, Sessions, Projects, Decisions, Research, category folders).
# In Docker this is /data/vault inside the container, bind-mounted from
# ${OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH:-./vault} on the host.
OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH=./vault

# ─── Logging ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# DEBUG | INFO | WARNING | ERROR | CRITICAL
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# json    — machine-parseable; what production should use
# console — coloured + human-friendly; what dev should use
LOG_FORMAT=console

# ─── ARQ / dedup tuning (optional) ─────────────────────────────────

ARQ_QUEUE_NAME=neuralscape:queue
ARQ_MAX_RETRIES=3
ARQ_JOB_TIMEOUT=300

DEDUP_SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD=0.95
DEDUP_BATCH_SIZE=100

# LLM retry budget for transient 503/429 from Gemini (exponential backoff).
LLM_MAX_RETRIES=3
LLM_RETRY_BASE_DELAY=1.0
LLM_RETRY_MAX_DELAY=30.0

# ─── Identity defaults (rarely needed) ─────────────────────────────

DEFAULT_USER_ID=default_user

# ─── Extensions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Comma-separated dotted paths to extra extension modules to auto-load
# alongside the built-in conversation_compiler. Leave empty unless
# you've written one.
NEURALSCAPE_EXTENSIONS=

# ─── Wiki synthesizer ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Master switch. When true, the cron (every WIKI_SYNTHESIZER_CRON_HOURS,
# default 6h) builds topical wiki pages from shared memories into
# ${OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH}/Wiki/, and the admin endpoints
# `POST /v1/admin/synthesize` + `GET .../status` become operational.
# Defaults to false — the synthesizer stays dark until you opt in.
# Output layout is:
#   Wiki/<project_id>/<TypeGroup>/<Category>.md   (per-project shared)
#   Wiki/global/<TypeGroup>/<Category>.md         (cross-project shared)
# The "Project" type-group is renamed to "General" everywhere.
WIKI_SYNTHESIZER_ENABLED=false

# How often the synthesizer cron runs, in hours (1-24). Default: 6.
# WIKI_SYNTHESIZER_CRON_HOURS=6

# Hard ceiling on source memories aggregated into a single page (1-500).
# Default: 50. Pages over the cap log a "split needed" warning; v1
# won't auto-split.
# WIKI_SYNTHESIZER_MAX_MEMORIES_PER_PAGE=50

# Override the Gemini model used for incremental merges. Empty string
# means inherit the core GEMINI_LLM_MODEL.
# WIKI_SYNTHESIZER_GEMINI_MODEL=

# Per-call Gemini timeout in seconds (30-1800). Default: 300.
# WIKI_SYNTHESIZER_GEMINI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300

# Retries per Gemini call (0-5). 1s/2s/4s exponential backoff. Default: 2.
# WIKI_SYNTHESIZER_GEMINI_MAX_RETRIES=2

# ─── Cloudflare tunnel (deploy-only) ───────────────────────────────
#
# Only relevant when running the optional ``tunnel`` compose profile
# (``docker compose --profile tunnel up -d cloudflared``). Provision
# a tunnel in the Cloudflare dashboard (Zero Trust → Networks →
# Tunnels), copy the connector token, and paste it here. Cloudflared
# joins the default compose network and routes incoming traffic to
# ``neuralscape:8199`` based on the public hostname configured in the
# dashboard.
CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=
